# config/defconfigs/rpi5.config — Raspberry Pi 5 (BCM2712, aarch64) — Edge profile
#
# Target: 4x Cortex-A76 (Armv8.2-A). BOARD_RPI5 sets the Armv8.2 level, which
# makes LSE atomics and CRC32 required; PAuth, BTI, MTE and SVE are not offered
# by this core and default to never. The board is selectable so it is visible
# in `make config`, but it is NOT ported: `make rpi5` stops with a message that
# names what is missing (a GIC-400 / GICv2 interrupt-controller backend, the
# BCM2712 PL011 debug UART as console, and firmware boot).
#
# Regenerate with:  make defconfig-rpi5 && make savedefconfig
CONFIG_ARCH_AARCH64=y
CONFIG_BOARD_RPI5=y
CONFIG_NR_CPUS=4
# CONFIG_DOMAIN_ROBOT=y (wave 11, DOMAIN): like vf2 and k1, this board image
# is the robot worked example (the Pi 5 is the robot's aarch64 board). The
# domain is what links the robot crates (kernel feature `domain-robot`);
# `make config` from scratch defaults to DOMAIN_GENERIC.
CONFIG_DOMAIN_ROBOT=y
